MGED command regression tests
=============================

Each .mged script runs in a fresh database and working directory named for
its test.  Fixed-name output files therefore cannot come from another test
or an earlier run.  Databases and caches are removed after a successful run;
the saved-view fixture database is retained until its consumer finishes.

The driver sources each script as one Tcl command.  This preserves command
substitutions in assertions and prevents asynchronous event servicing from
reading the next scripted stdin command.  Database name patterns must be
expanded explicitly with commands such as:

    prefix has_ {*}[expand prefix*]

Do not depend on MGED's interactive glob preprocessing to expand patterns
or evaluate assertions.  regression_assert and regression_check_vector in
regression_resources.tcl provide shared assertion and numeric comparison
helpers.  Check resulting geometry, references, visibility, or view state
where practical, rather than merely listing objects or printing a result.

An uncaught Tcl error prints its error stack and suppresses the driver's
completion marker.  The CMake harness requires that marker and a successful
process status, and rejects explicit FAIL: output.  MGED's process status
alone does not reliably indicate Tcl command failures.  Expected errors
must be caught and checked by the test; matching every occurrence of ERROR
would incorrectly reject intentional negative cases and empty primitives.
regress-mged-harness verifies error, assertion, printed-failure, incomplete
input, quit, and immediate exit detection using the actual frontend.

Shared file fixtures
--------------------

CTest declares saveview as the setup for the mged_saved_view fixture and
loadview as its consumer.  loadview opens the producer's database and checks
the saved orientation, scale, displayed objects, and projected center.
Orthographic saveview may move the ray origin along the viewing axis, so
exact equality of the three-dimensional view center is not required.

Similarly, plot produces the mged_plot fixture consumed by overlay.  Both
fixtures have cleanup tests that run after their consumers, even when a
consumer fails.  Selecting either consumer automatically selects its setup
and cleanup, including when tests run in parallel:

    ctest --test-dir build -R '^regress-mged_(loadview|overlay)$' -j4 --output-on-failure

Fixture paths are supplied by the driver through regression_fixture_directory.
Do not recreate a missing shared fixture in a consumer: failure to prepare
the input must remain visible to the test runner.
